    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fair Oaks is a town located across both Rogers and Wagoner counties in Oklahoma.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_Oaks%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "L. Robson, owner of a large ranch in Wagoner County, incorporated Fair Oaks as a town in 1966.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_Oaks%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fair Oaks began with only two hundred acres of land and about twenty residents at the time of its incorporation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_Oaks%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fair Oaks expanded its boundaries significantly in 1969 by adding fifteen thousand acres of land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_Oaks%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fair Oaks was incorporated partly to protect its residents from being annexed by the expanding city of Tulsa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fair_oaks_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A master-planned development on the historic Robson Ranch land aims to bring economic revitalization to Fair Oaks through sustainable design.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
